---
/*
 * All sources at a glance: every entry of the licence record in one list, by
 * family, made from data/dataPages.ts. A row's name, what it is and the
 * opening of its licence line are the record's words; the counts are counted.
 */
import DocLink from '../../../components/DocLink.astro';
import DocTable from '../../../components/DocTable.astro';
import { DATA_ENTRIES, DATA_FAMILIES_USED } from '../../../data/dataPages';
import { REPO_BLOB } from '../../../data/siteIdentity';
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { fitText } from '../../../utils/fitText';
import { formatDate } from '../../../utils/formatDate';
import { licenceLead } from '../../../utils/licenceLead';
import { plainText } from '../../../utils/plainText';

/** As much of an entry's "What" as a row of the list holds. */
const WHAT_MAX = 150;
const families = DATA_FAMILIES_USED.map((family) => ({
  ...family,
  entries: DATA_ENTRIES.filter((entry) => entry.family === family.id),
}));
const dates = [...new Set(DATA_ENTRIES.map((entry) => entry.checked))].sort();
const unverified = DATA_ENTRIES.filter((entry) => entry.record.bullets['Not verified']).length;
---

<Docs
  path="/docs/data/"
  description="Every catalogue, image, model, font and piece of code skymap is built from, by family, each with the opening of its licence and a page of its own."
  headings={families.map((family) => ({ depth: 2, slug: family.id, text: family.name }))}
  factIds={[]}
>
  <p>
    A source, here, is anything in skymap that somebody else made: a catalogue, a picture, a height map, a 3D model, a typeface, a
    function we ported, a service the app asks while it runs. There are {DATA_ENTRIES.length} of them, in {families.length} families. A few
    entries at the end are our own files, listed because they hold other people’s figures.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each row gives the source’s name, what it is, and the opening words of its licence line in our record. The name leads to the full
    text: the terms as the rights holder states them, the credit it asks for, where its files enter the build and what it becomes in the
    app. How the files become what the app loads is on <DocLink href="/docs/data/pipeline/">From catalogue to pixels</DocLink>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The record is one file in the repository, the <a href={`${REPO_BLOB}/ATTRIBUTIONS.md`}>attributions file</a>, and these pages are
    made from it each time the site is built. Its terms are quoted from the rights holders’ own pages as we read them{' '}
    {dates.length === 1 ? `on ${formatDate(dates[0]!)}` : `between ${formatDate(dates[0]!)} and ${formatDate(dates.at(-1)!)}`}; each
    entry’s page gives its date and the pages read. For {unverified} entries something could not be opened that day, and the entry’s page
    says what. The pages state terms. They are not legal advice.
  </p>
  <p>
    A picture or film made with skymap carries the terms of every source visible in it. What that means for reusing our own pictures is
    under <DocLink href="/about/#press">Pictures and their terms</DocLink> on the About page, and the credit line each source asks for
    is on the <DocLink href="/docs/credits/">credits page</DocLink>.
  </p>

  {
    families.map((family) => (
      <>
        <h2 id={family.id}>{family.name}</h2>
        <p>
          {family.about}{' '}
          {family.pages === 'one' ? (
            <>
              These {family.entries.length} share <DocLink href={`/docs/data/${family.id}/`}>one page</DocLink>.
            </>
          ) : (
            `${family.entries.length} ${family.entries.length === 1 ? 'source' : 'sources'}.`
          )}
        </p>
        <DocTable
          cols="detail"
          head={['Source', 'What it is', 'Licence']}
          rows={family.entries.map((entry) => [
            { href: entry.href, label: entry.title },
            fitText(plainText(entry.record.bullets.What ?? ''), WHAT_MAX),
            licenceLead(entry.record.bullets.Licence ?? ''),
          ])}
        />
      </>
    ))
  }
</Docs>
